<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Air LaunchAgent for a factory kubectl port-forward tunnel (PQ-3).

  Every unattended factory drain — the Temporal worker and the dispatcher's
  substrate calls alike — sits on top of a bare `kubectl port-forward`. Before
  this template existed, a dead tunnel stalled the factory silently: nothing
  restarted it, and the worker's own tunnel-loss alert only reaches a log file
  when DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL is unset. KeepAlive here means launchd restarts the
  forward without operator action; it does not fix that alert gap.

  ProgramArguments invokes kubectl directly, not through /bin/sh -c: a tunnel
  needs no env sourcing, no cwd, and no secrets, so there is nothing a shell
  would add.

  Do not put secrets in this plist. LaunchAgent plists in ~/Library/LaunchAgents
  are world-readable enough that credentials must stay out of ProgramArguments
  entirely. A kubeconfig PATH is not a secret, so when the installer is given
  a kubeconfig flag it renders an explicit "kubeconfig PATH" argument pair
  below; this host deliberately has no default kubectl context, so relying on
  an "ambient kubeconfig" here means every launchd-spawned restart fails
  identically forever. When no kubeconfig flag is given, install-tunnel has
  already confirmed a usable default context exists before writing this file,
  so the omission here is a verified choice, not an assumption.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>$LABEL</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
$PROGRAM_ARGUMENTS_XML
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>10</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>$STDOUT_PATH</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>$STDERR_PATH</string>
</dict>
</plist>
